</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/247ad3fa-cebc-11f1-9f6f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-090607-090912-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/247ad3fa-cebc-11f1-9f6f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-090607-090912-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29842248-cebc-11f1-8576-1b51f8bed30c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:40:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu vows to ‘destroy’ Hebron after 2 soldiers killed in ‘terrorist attack’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-netanyahu-orders-army-to-prepare-for-full-west-bank-closure-after-attack</link><description>
Israel’s Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday vowed to “destroy” the Palestinian city of Hebron in the occupied West Bank after two Israeli soldiers were killed at a military checkpoint there. The two gunmen were also killed in the “terrorist attack”, the army said.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0f92bb8-ceb8-11f1-a0a6-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296286800872.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0f92bb8-ceb8-11f1-a0a6-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296286800872.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b0629b2-ceb8-11f1-a70d-459e24a86637</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:35:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0f92bb8-ceb8-11f1-a0a6-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296286800872.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Israel's Ben-Gvir shares AI videos mocking Gazans as 'donkeys' and sending them to Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261022-israel-s-ben-gvir-shares-ai-videos-mocking-gazans-as-donkeys-and-sending-them-to-paris</link><description>
Israel's far-right minister Itamar Ben-Gvir is using AI-generated videos to mock Palestinians and push political messages ahead of the Israeli general election, including videos magically transporting Gazans to Paris or calling them "donkeys" for choosing to stay. One video has sparked an online spat with France. Artificial intelligence is playing a growing role in the campaign, with parties using deepfakes, bots and AI-generated content, raising concerns about disinformation and the technology's influence on voters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e919d896-ce4e-11f1-bdb8-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/thumbnail-icon.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e919d896-ce4e-11f1-bdb8-7967b15eed96/w:1024/p:16x9/thumbnail-icon.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27c0a7b8-ce50-11f1-99a0-0d0ef307c500</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:38:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ahead of US and Israeli elections, 3-day joint attack on Iran 'would not radically change conflict'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Federico Donelli, Associate Professor of International Relations in the Department of Political and Social Sciences at the University of Trieste in Italy. Can another three days of military strikes achieve what eight months of confrontation have failed to deliver? Donelli challenges the assumption that a short, intensive offensive would necessarily produce a decisive political outcome. He argues, "the real question is whether military pressure is intended to constrain Iran's capacity, or to pressure Iran to sit on the table." And whether they can translate that capacity into a sustainable political outcome without provoking a wider regional crisis. Regardless, Donelli reminds us that "Iran still has leverage over the US."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c66a7ce-ce2d-11f1-9d8f-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-152144-153307-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c66a7ce-ce2d-11f1-9d8f-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-152144-153307-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">620ff428-ce2d-11f1-8eed-af0e081df335</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:36:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Reports show US and Israel are planning new strikes on Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-reports-show-us-and-israel-plan-new-strikes-on-iran</link><description>
Reports claim that the US and Israel have ramped up military drills and planned new strikes in Iran, potentially targeting energy sites, drone facilities and missile arsenals. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe660f46-ce29-11f1-adff-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d432d452.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe660f46-ce29-11f1-adff-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d432d452.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb5763c4-ce26-11f1-9bb3-7ff061e04dbf</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:34:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
